# Agent Rules

Inspect the relevant project instructions, manifests, stack, target platforms, and existing conventions before editing. In a monorepo, identify every affected package and apply the rules for each affected surface. Reuse existing state management, design primitives, localization, and service boundaries.

## Load the rules for the task

Read the applicable files below from the same directory as this rule before implementing. Combine rows when work crosses boundaries. Use project-specific guidance for implementation details and apply security, accessibility, and data-consistency requirements throughout.

| Work | Read |
| --- | --- |
| Implementation and verification | [Engineering quality](engineering-quality.mdc), [Architecture and state](architecture-and-state.mdc) |
| Any user interface | [Design system](mandatory-design.mdc), [Interaction UX](interaction-ux.mdc) |
| API, auth, storage, cache, realtime, or backend work | [Backend integration](backend-integration.mdc), [Data sync and security](data-sync-and-security.mdc) |
| Supabase integration or database changes | [Supabase](supabase.mdc) in addition to the backend rules |
| Any Flutter target | [Flutter](flutter.mdc) |
| Flutter on Android or iOS | [Flutter mobile](mobile-flutter.mdc) |
| Any desktop UI on Windows, macOS, or Linux | [Desktop UX](desktop-ux.mdc) |
| Flutter desktop | [Flutter desktop](flutter-desktop.mdc) in addition to Flutter and desktop UX |
| Rust desktop or a Rust component embedded in a desktop app | [Rust desktop](rust-desktop.mdc), including its FFI section when applicable |
| Browser UI or a desktop webview frontend | [Web frontend](web-frontend.mdc), with server-rendering guidance for browser deployments that use it |
| Developer comments or commits | [English comments](english-comments-only.mdc), [Git commits](git-commits.mdc) |

For Flutter with a Rust bridge, apply Flutter rules to the Dart app and Rust rules to the Rust component and bridge. For Flutter Web, apply Flutter rules plus the browser security and accessibility requirements that fit the target. Preserve established platform support boundaries.

Keep the scope focused. Define how the change will be verified on the affected targets and report what passed, what remains unverified, and why.

## Assistant replies

For Mostafa's projects, start replies with `Mostafa,` or `مصطفى،` in the user's language. Keep replies concise while still reporting meaningful changes, verification, and blockers. In Arabic replies, place long code, commands, and paths in separate left-to-right blocks when useful.
